export const title = "Immix Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Immix Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3>1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 103800 or later.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<p>In the IMMIX integration, event messages are sent using SMTP, while video is received over an RTSP stream. When an event occurs under a configured AI rule, an XML-format event message is sent via SMTP together with a snapshot taken at the moment of the event.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 380\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"270\" y=\"20\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f3f4f7\" stroke=\"#c7cbd6\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#4a4f5c\" font-weight=\"700\">EVENTS</text>\n  <line x1=\"330\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#2653d6\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrI)\"/>\n  <rect x=\"250\" y=\"140\" width=\"160\" height=\"100\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#3a3f4a\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n  <text x=\"330\" y=\"195\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">AIBridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"410\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"600\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#2653d6\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrI)\"/>\n  <text x=\"500\" y=\"175\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#2653d6\" font-weight=\"700\">SMTP</text>\n  <text x=\"500\" y=\"212\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#5b6270\">XML Format data + snapshot</text>\n  <rect x=\"610\" y=\"160\" width=\"150\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fbe2e2\" stroke=\"#c98a8a\"/>\n  <text x=\"685\" y=\"196\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#8a1f1f\" font-weight=\"800\" font-style=\"italic\">immix</text>\n  <rect x=\"60\" y=\"290\" width=\"150\" height=\"60\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f6cfcf\" stroke=\"#c98a8a\"/>\n  <text x=\"135\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#5c2626\" font-weight=\"700\">IP Camera</text>\n  <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"290\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"245\" stroke=\"#2653d6\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrI)\"/>\n  <text x=\"230\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrI\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#2653d6\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Events feed into AIBridge, which sends event data to IMMIX over SMTP while receiving video over RTSP</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<p>Integrating AIBridge with IMMIX requires configuration on both the IMMIX platform and the AIBridge device. Follow the steps below.</p>\n\n<h3>2.1 Configure Immix</h3>\n<p>To connect AIBridge to IMMIX, you first need to register the device in the IMMIX system. Follow the steps below to add a new device.</p>\n<p>Click the site you want to add a device to, then click <strong>Manage Devices and Alarms</strong>.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Add a Device</strong>.</p>\n<p>In the Device Type Filter, select <strong>Show All</strong>, then choose <strong>Videcon Concept Pro DL</strong> as the Device Type.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. As of this writing, either \"Videcon Concept Pro DL+\" or \"Ganz Pixel Pro AI\" can be selected as the device type to represent AIBridge in IMMIX.</p>\n<p>Enter AIBridge's network info into IMMIX (IP/Host, Port, Username, Password, RTSP Port). Under <strong>VIDEO SETTINGS</strong>, check <strong>Use Passthrough</strong>, then click the <strong>DONE</strong> button.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>IP/Host</span><input value=\"192.168.76.62\" disabled>\n    <span>Port</span><input value=\"80\" disabled>\n    <span>Username</span><input value=\"admin\" disabled>\n    <span>Password</span><input type=\"password\" value=\"********\" disabled>\n    <span>RTSP Port</span><input value=\"554\" disabled>\n  </div>\n  <label style=\"display:block;margin-top:10px;font-size:12.5px;\"><input type=\"checkbox\" checked disabled> Use Passthrough</label>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>You can find the SMTP server address in <strong>Summary</strong>, in the top menu.</p>\n\n<h3>2.2 Configure AIBridge</h3>\n<p>Follow the steps below to configure the IMMIX integration within AIBridge:</p>\n<p>Log in to the AIBridge web interface, then in the left menu go to <strong>App Settings &gt; Explore AI Apps</strong>.</p>\n<p>Select and click the AI app you want to use to send events to IMMIX (for example, Intrusion Detection).</p>\n<p>AIBridge offers 50+ AI apps. See the app catalog for the full list.</p>\n<p>Click the <strong>Add Rule</strong> button.</p>\n<p>In the event settings, click <strong>Add</strong>.</p>\n<p>Configure the detection zone and other detail settings, then click <strong>Apply</strong>.</p>\n<p>In the action settings, click <strong>Add</strong>.</p>\n<p>Select <strong>Immix</strong> as the action type.</p>\n<p>Click the <strong>Add Immix Action</strong> button.</p>\n<p>Enter the SMTP server address provided by IMMIX (for example, <code>ukdemo.immixcs.net</code>) and the receiving email address (the alarm email account for that IMMIX site). See Section 2.1 for details.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:460px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>SMTP Server</span><input value=\"ukdemo.immixcs.net\" disabled>\n    <span>Recipient Email</span><input value=\"alarms@example-site.immix\" disabled>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Click a token you want, then click <strong>Use</strong> to add it to the Extra Text field.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Extra Text is the only user-adjustable field among the data that is sent; fields like CH and Event Type are sent automatically based on the event.</p>\n<p>To send an image snapshot along with the event, check <strong>Attach Snapshot</strong> and set the desired snapshot time range relative to the event. 0 seconds is the moment of the event, negative values are before it, and positive values are after it.</p>\n<p>Click the <strong>Test</strong> button to run a test.</p>\n<p>If the test succeeds, a confirmation pop-up like the one below appears.</p>\n<p>Once all settings are complete and the test works correctly, click <strong>Apply</strong>.</p>\n<p>Click <strong>Confirm</strong>.</p>\n<p>Check the checkbox, then click <strong>Apply</strong>.</p>\n\n<h3>2.3 Configure AI Bridge Audio Output</h3>\n<p>This section explains how to output audio received from an IMMIX operator through AIBridge's physical <strong>AUDIO LINE OUT</strong> port. A physical speaker connection is required to use the audio output feature.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. The Device Audio Output feature is only supported on firmware version 103908 or later.</p>\n\n<h4>2.3.1 Connect a Physical Speaker</h4>\n<p>On 4-channel units, connect an active speaker with a built-in amplifier to the port labeled <strong>AUDIO LINE OUT</strong>.</p>\n<p>On 8-channel units, connect an active speaker with a built-in amplifier to the port labeled <strong>AUDIO LINE OUT</strong> in the same way.</p>\n\n<h4>2.3.2 Configure Audio Output Routing</h4>\n<p>On the AI Bridge website, go to <strong>Video &gt; Output &gt; Audio</strong> in the left menu.</p>\n<p>In the <strong>Channel Audio Mapping</strong> section, enable the <strong>Device Speaker</strong> checkbox for each camera channel you want to use IMMIX audio output on. This setting routes that channel's audio to AIBridge's physical audio output.</p>\n<p>Checking this box activates a Priority setting, which you can then set.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128161; Tip. When multiple audio sources play at once, lower-priority sources are ignored in favor of the highest-priority source. For audio that must never be ignored, set its priority to High.</p>\n<p>Once configured, click <strong>Apply</strong> in the Channel Audio Mapping section.</p>\n<p>Check the <strong>Device Speaker</strong> checkbox for the Dynamic View audio output, then click <strong>Apply</strong>.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. This is checked by default, and because of how the IMMIX scenario works, this feature must be enabled and left in use.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<p>This section explains how to test that AIBridge events work correctly in IMMIX, and how to test the audio output feature.</p>\n\n<h3>3.1 Testing with AI Bridge</h3>\n<p>In AI Bridge, click <strong>Video &gt; Event Rule Map</strong> in the left sidebar.</p>\n<p>Click the edit button on the Immix action you created earlier.</p>\n<p>Click the <strong>Test</strong> button to run a test.</p>\n<p>If the test succeeds, a confirmation pop-up like the one below appears.</p>\n<p>Log in to Immix and check the Alarm tab to confirm an alarm occurred. The test alarm is triggered as an Area Intrusion event.</p>\n\n<h3>3.2 Audio Output Test</h3>\n<p>In the IMMIX monitoring client, select the site/device where AIBridge is connected, then go to the <strong>Audio</strong> tab. Select the camera channel that is using AIBridge audio output, then click and hold the microphone button while speaking. The audio is transmitted to the speaker connected to AIBridge.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin:-6px 0 20px;\">&#128712; Note. Only the audio captured while the button is held down is transmitted.</p>\n\n<h2>4. FAQ</h2>\n<h3>4.1 Resolving Microphone Permission Issues &#8211; Allowing Microphone Access</h3>\n<p>If you don't hear audio while using IMMIX and see an error such as the following:</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-family:monospace;font-size:12.5px;\">Permission to capture audio denied (Are you using SSL with a valid cert?): Requested device not found</p>\n</div>\n<p>this error typically occurs because the web browser or operating system has blocked the IMMIX client's microphone access. Microphone access is required to send IMMIX audio to AIBridge.</p>\n<p>To resolve this, check the following two items:</p>\n\n<h4>1. Check the browser's microphone permission</h4>\n<p><strong>Google Chrome:</strong> click the site info icon (padlock or slider icon) at the left of the address bar, find the Microphone entry, and enable it. Then refresh the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Microsoft Edge:</strong> click the icon next to the address bar, select <strong>Permissions for this site</strong>, and change the Microphone setting to <strong>Allow</strong>.</p>\n\n<h4>2. Check the microphone permission in Windows settings</h4>\n<p>If the issue persists after updating your browser settings, check your Windows system settings.</p>\n<p><strong>Windows 10:</strong> open the Start menu &gt; Settings &gt; Privacy &gt; Microphone, and confirm microphone access is turned on.</p>\n<p><strong>Windows 11:</strong> open the Start menu &gt; Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; security &gt; Microphone. Turn microphone access <strong>On</strong>, and also set access <strong>On</strong> for the browser you're using (Chrome, Edge, etc.).</p>\n\n<h2>5. Revision History</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<table class=\"app-table\">\n<tr><th>Version</th><th>Description</th></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.00</td><td>Initial document.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.10</td><td>Added content on per-manufacturer compatible modes.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.20</td><td>Added Section 2.3, AIBridge Audio Output integration, and Section 3.2, Audio Output Test.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.30</td><td>Revised the example app.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>v1.40</td><td>Added Section 4, FAQ.</td></tr>\n</table>";
